# basePath DesignAndv2
// And v2

::Intro
@trigger    OnDesignSetupComplete
$set temp:hintGiven = 0
{@PAL} Logic Gates make computers possible! They never have empty outputs.\nAND outputs HI only if A and B are HI.

::Hints
@trigger    OnSingleTestComplete
@when       result == "failure"
$if temp:hintGiven == 0
    {@PAL}  Hint: Use A and B to control Gates. Use constants to send signals to X.
    $set temp:hintGiven == 1
$elseif temp:hintGiven == 1
    {@PAL}  Hint: If both A and B are HI, allow HI to flow to X. You can use a transistor with two Gates.
    $set temp:hintGiven == 2
$elseif temp:hintGiven == 2
    {@PAL}  Hint: If A is LO, allow LO to flow to X. If B is LO, allow LO to flow X.
    $set temp:hintGiven == 3
$elseif temp:hintGiven == 3
    {@PAL}  Hint: Use separate gates for A LO and B LO to prevent Unstable signals.
    $set temp:hintGiven == 0
$endif